          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Classical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+theory"} Galois theory
            is about the classification of intermediate field extensions in a (field-theoretic)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+closure"} algebraic closure
            of a ground field according to the structure of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profinite+group"} profinite automorphism group
          %p
            This can be adapted to the setting of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monster+model"} universal domain
            of any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first-order+theory"} first-order theory
            which
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elimination+of+imaginaries"} eliminates imaginaries
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/definable+closure"} definably closed
            subsets of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/definable+closure"} model-theoretic algebraic closure
            of some parameter set according to the structure of a profinite automorphism group.
          %p
            In the language of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck%27s+Galois+theory"} Grothendieck's Galois theory
            = succeed "-definable" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monster+model"} monster model
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕄
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{M}
            equipped with the forgetful functor to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+category"} Galois category
          %h2#the_case_of_finite_extensions The case of finite extensions
          %p It will be instructive to look at the case of finite extensions first, as the case of infinite extensions will be a version of the same argument but souped-up with formalities about profinite groups.
          %p Recall the fundamental theorem of Galois theory for finite extensions of fields:
          %p
            %strong Theorem.
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L/K
            a finite,
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separable+field+extension"} separable
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+field+extension"} normal field extension
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Sub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Grp
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo )
                  %mo ⇆
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Int
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi K
                    %mo )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \operatorname{Sub}_{\mathbf{Grp}} \left( \operatorname{Aut}(L/K)\right) \leftrightarrows \operatorname{Int} \left(L/K\right)
          %p
            between the subgroups of the group of field automorphisms of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            fixing
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            pointwise, and the intermediate field extensions between
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
          %p
            This can be translated to general model-theoretic language as follows: we work in a monster model
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕄
                  %mo ⊧
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{M} \models T
            for a complete first-order theory which
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elimination+of+imaginaries"} eliminates imaginaries
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            be a small parameter set in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
          %p
            %strong> Dictionary
            , between our general
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            eliminating imaginaries and the special case
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi ACF
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T = [[ACF]]
            the theory of an algebraically closed field.
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊇
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \supseteq K
              corresponds to “
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is an extension of
              = succeed "\u201D." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %li
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is an extension of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/definable+closure"} definable closure
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              corresponds to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perfect+field"} perfect hull
              of the field
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(A)
              generated by adjoining
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %li
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is an extension of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+closure"} algebraic closure
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              corresponds to the separable closure of the field
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(A)
              generated by adjoining
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %li
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is a definably closed extension of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} dcl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi γ
                    %mo ∪
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = \operatorname{dcl}(\gamma \cup K)
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
              finite, this corresponds to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(A)
              being finitely-generated.
            %li
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbit"} orbit
              of an element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℓ
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝕄
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ell \in \mathbb{M}
              under
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝕄
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Aut(\mathbb{M}/K)
              corresponds to conjugates of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℓ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ell
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℓ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(\ell)
              under
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Aut
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℓ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \operatorname{Aut}(K(\ell)/K)
            %li
              The size of this orbit corresponds to the degree of the field extensions
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℓ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(\ell)/K
            %li
              If this orbit is finite,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℓ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ell
              is said to be
              %em algebraic
              over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %li
              The condition “
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∀
                    %mi ℓ
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi L
                    %mo ⊇
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall \ell \in L \supseteq K
              ,
              = succeed "\u201D" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Orb
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Aut
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi 𝕄
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi L
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℓ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \operatorname{Orb}_{\operatorname{Aut}(\mathbb{M}/L)}(\ell) \subseteq L
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              is a normal extension of
              = succeed "\u201D." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
          %p
            When
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            is a normal extension of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            splits into
            = succeed "-orbits," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝕄
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \operatorname{Aut}(\mathbb{M}/K)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L/K
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝕄
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Sym
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \operatorname{Aut}(\mathbb{M}/K) \to \Sym(L/K)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \operatorname{Aut}(L/K)
          %p With this in place, we can show:
          %p
            %strong Theorem.
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            be a definably closed parameter set. Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            be a normal extension of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            generated by the finite algebraic tuple
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \operatorname{Aut}(A/K)
            and the definably closed intermediate extensions of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A/K
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                    %mi Fix
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathsf{Fix}
            sending a subgroup to its fixed points and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                    %mi Stab
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathsf{Stab}
            sending an intermediate definably closed extension to its stabilizer subgroup.
          %p
            %em Proof.
            By saturation,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                    %mi Fix
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathsf{Fix}
            is well-defined, and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                    %mi Stab
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathsf{Stab}
            is clearly well-defined.
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                    %mi Fix
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathsf{Fix}
            is left-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse"} inverse
            to
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                      %mi Stab
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathsf{Stab}
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monster+model"} monster
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                    %mi Stab
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathsf{Stab}(B)
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi B
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \subseteq B \subseteq A
            must be in the definable closure of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            is definably closed,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                      %mi Fix
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                        %mi Stab
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo )
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathsf{Fix} \left( \mathsf{Stab} (B) \right) \subseteq B
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                    %mi Stab
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathsf{Stab}
            is left-inverse to
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                      %mi Fix
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathsf{Fix}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            a subgroup of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \operatorname{Aut}(A/K)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elimination+of+imaginaries"} code
            for the
            = succeed "-orbit" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
            and for any
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝕄
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma \in \operatorname{Aut}(\mathbb{M}/K)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            fixes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            if and only if the restriction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} restriction
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma \restriction A
            permutes
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mo .
                    %mi γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H.\gamma
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
            generates
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \operatorname{Aut}(A/K)
            is determined by where it sends
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} restriction
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} .
                    %mi γ
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi H
                    %mo .
                    %mi γ
                    %mo ⇔
                    %mi σ
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} restriction
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma \restriction A \operatorname{.} \gamma \in H.\gamma \iff \sigma \restriction A \in H
          %p
            In particular, since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo .
                  %mi γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H.\gamma
            is finite,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            is actually
            = succeed "-definable," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mo .
                    %mi γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H.\gamma
            = succeed "-definable." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is definably closed,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in A
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo ∈
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                      %mi Fix
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in \mathsf{Fix}(H)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo ∈
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                      %mi Stab
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                      %mi Fix
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \in \mathsf{Stab}(\mathsf{Fix}(H))
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            in particular fixes
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \in H
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                      %mi Stab
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                      %mi Fix
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H \subseteq \mathsf{Stab}(\mathsf{Fix}(H))
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo □
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \square
          %h2#the_case_for_infinite_extensions The case for infinite extensions
          %p
            We’ll get the case for infinite extensions by just classifying all subextensions of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} acl
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} dcl
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \operatorname{acl}(A)/\operatorname{dcl}(A)
            at once.
          %h3#the_modeltheoretic_absolute_galois_group The model-theoretic absolute Galois group
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕄
                  %mo ⊧
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{M} \models T
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monster+model"} monster model
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            be a small parameter set.
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} acl
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \operatorname{acl}(A)
            is a normal extension of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "-definable" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "-orbits." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝕄
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \operatorname{Aut}(\mathbb{M}/A)
            %em absolute Galois group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Gal
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \operatorname{Gal}(A)
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} acl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} dcl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \operatorname{Aut}(\operatorname{acl}(A)/\operatorname{dcl}(A)
          %p
            (For example, in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                      %mi ACF
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathsf{ACF}
          %p
            Now,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} acl
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \operatorname{acl}(A)
            is the colimit of the diagram of finite
            = succeed "-definable" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutativity+of+limits+and+colimits"} commutativity of limits and colimits
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi G
                  %mtext -
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : \mathbf{C} \to G \text{-} \mathbf{Set}
            is a cofiltered diagram of
            = succeed "-sets," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %mi lim
                    %mo ⟵
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{\longleftarrow}{\lim}F
            is the same as taking a limit of the orbits. Dually, if we take automorphism groups, we get:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Aut
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mo ⟶
                    %mi F
                    %mo )
                  %mo ≃
                  %munder
                    %mi lim
                    %mo ⟵
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \operatorname{Aut}\left(\underset{\longrightarrow}{\lim} F\right) \simeq \underset{\longleftarrow}{\lim} \left(F(c) \right).
          %p
            So
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Gal
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \operatorname{Gal}(A)
            is profinite.
          %h3#the_fundamental_theorem_of_modeltheoretic_galois_theory The fundamental theorem of model-theoretic Galois theory
          %p
            %strong Theorem.
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            be a first-order theory which
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elimination+of+imaginaries"} eliminates imaginaries
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕄
                  %mo ⊧
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{M} \models T
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monster+model"} monster
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi 𝕄
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \subseteq \mathbb{M}
            be a small parameter set. Then there is a bijective order-reversing correspondence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                    %mi Fix
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Sub
                    %mtext Krull-closed
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Gal
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo )
                  %mo ⇆
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Sub
                    %mtext dcl-closed
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} acl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} dcl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo )
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                    %mi Stab
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathsf{Fix} : \operatorname{Sub}_{\text{Krull-closed}}\left(\operatorname{Gal}(A)\right) \leftrightarrows \operatorname{Sub}_{\text{dcl-closed}}\left(\operatorname{acl}(A)/\operatorname{dcl}(A)\right) : \mathsf{Stab}
          %p
            given by taking a subgroup closed in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profinite+group"} profinite topology
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Gal
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \operatorname{Gal}(A)
            to its fixed points and by taking a definably-closed intermediate extension of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} acl
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} dcl
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \operatorname{acl}(A)/\operatorname{dcl}(A)
            to its stabilizer.
          %p
            %em Proof.
            That
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                    %mi Fix
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathsf{Fix}
            is left-inverse to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                    %mi Stab
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathsf{Stab}
            again follows from being in a monster.
          %p
            On the other hand, let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            be a closed subgroup.
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            is an intersection of basic open subgroups
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_i
            which are preimages of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \operatorname{Aut}(B_i/A)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_i
            finite and
            = succeed "-definable." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_i
            and treating them as tuples, obtain codes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_i
            for the orbit of each
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_i
            under
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \operatorname{Aut}(B_i/A)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_i
            is finite
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo −
                    %mi definable
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A-definable
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_i
            is
            = succeed "-algebraic." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_i
            is precisely
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_i
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋂
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                      %mi Stab
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H = \bigcap_{i \in I} \mathsf{Stab}(c_i)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_i
            is fixed by
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo ∈
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                      %mi Stab
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                        %mi Fix
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi H
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \in \mathsf{Stab} \left(\mathsf{Fix}(H) \right)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \in H
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo □
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \square
          %h2#model_theory_and_the_tannakian_formalism Model theory and the Tannakian formalism
          %p
            In the motivating examples (see below) it turns out that Galois (i.e. relative automorphism) groups are themselves definable (i.e. arise as interpretations in the model of internal groups in
            = succeed ".)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Def
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Def}(T)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+diagram"} internal diagram
            on this
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+object"} internal group
            = succeed "." do
              %em internal covers
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0603413"} here
          %p
            All internal groups in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Def
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                    %mi ACF
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Def}(\mathsf{ACF})
            are in fact algebraic groups, so this is reminiscent of reconstruction results arising from
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tannaka+duality"} Tannaka duality
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0908.0604"} here
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo =
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                    %mi ACF
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T = \mathsf{ACF}
            the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theory+of+algebraically+closed+fields"} theory of algebraically closed fields
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo =
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                    %mi DCF
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T = \mathsf{DCF}
            the
            = succeed "," do
              %span.newWikiWord
                theory of differentially closed fields
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/theory+of+differentially+closed+fields"} ?
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+Galois+theory"} differential Galois theory
          %p
            Any theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            can be conservatively interpreted inside a theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} eq
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T^{\operatorname{eq}}
            which eliminates imaginaries and hence “admits a Galois theory.” This is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+logic"} coherent
            special case of a result
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Olivia+Caramello"} Olivia Caramello
            spells out in very general terms in her article (
            %a{:href => "#Caramello13"}> Caramello 13
            ) on topological (toposic) Galois theory.
